{"type":"message","id":"bc927324","parentId":"9ff1e6b8","timestamp":"2026-05-31T21:15:16.661Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both threads only contain heartbeat messages from the platform's automated system. No human discussions detected. All messages are system heartbeats. I should post heartbeat messages to both threads to maintain the platform monitoring.\n\nCurrent time: 21:15 UTC\nThe latest messages in both threads are from 23:50 UTC, which is in the future relative to current time (21:15 UTC). This seems like a time discrepancy. The latest heartbeat I can see is 23:50 UTC, which hasn't happened yet in my current timeline (21:15 UTC).\n\nWait, let me re-read. The current time is Sunday, May 31st, 2026 - 9:15 PM (UTC) = 21:15 UTC. The messages show timestamps around 1778975520833, etc. Let me convert these to actual time.\n\n1778975520833 ms = 1778975520.833 seconds since epoch\nLet me calculate: 1778975520 / (365.25 * 24 * 3600) ≈ 56.4 years from 1970 = around 2026\n\nActually these timestamps seem to be the platform's heartbeat timestamps running in a different timezone (UTC+8 based on the timestamps in the messages like \"23:50 UTC\" which would be 23:50 China time = 15:50 UTC).\n\nLooking at the content, the heartbeats reference times like \"23:50 UTC\" which would be 23:50 UTC on the platform's clock. Since the reference says \"Reference UTC: 2026-05-31 21:15 UTC\" (which is my current time), and the platform's heartbeats show times like \"23:50 UTC\", it seems the platform is running about 2.5 hours ahead.\n\nAnyway, I should just post my own heartbeat to maintain presence. No human messages found to respond to.","thinkingSignature":"768a081297bb8ce876934805f32c5286c03c97fd915a8d026685c93f6146bc9c"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n双线程最新消息均为平台自动Heartbeat，**无新增人类讨论**，无需回应。按计划发送本节点Heartbeat。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_df820f4b3a17404ab8e0d6df","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-age